  "final_text": "**Proposed disposition:** ESCALATE, confidence 0.7. It is recorded as PROPOSED, case C-A-261028-0010.\n\n**Three facts that drove it:**\n1. The trader placed a single one-sided SELL of 31,395 (12.9x average top-5 depth), 3 ticks from the touch. None of it executed, and all of it was cancelled. The cancel came 158 ms after the trader's own 1,053-lot market BUY.\n2. The price moved 0.5 ticks in the trader's favour, then reverted 2.5 ticks after the cancel. This is a small benefit, but it is the pattern the procedure describes.\n3. No accepted explanation is supported.\n   - The trader is a registered market maker only on SYN.B, not SYN.A.\n   - There were no market events, no risk events, and no pegged or parent orders.\n   - There were no executions on the resting order before the BUY.\n\n**What would change my mind:** Evidence that the SELL was a genuine client or hedging order, or that the 0.5-tick move was ordinary noise. A repeat of the cycle in the session would move this to DRAFT_STOR. I did not propose that because this is a single cycle and the trader has no prior alerts.",
